th `{\"error\": \"threshold must be a non-negative integer\"}`. That covers `abc`, `-1`, `2.5`, an empty value, `+5`, a value with a leading space, and non-ASCII digits. I also reject a repeated `threshold` (`threshold=1&threshold=2`), because your spec didn't say what that should do. Say so if you'd rather it take one of the values.\n- **Other endpoints:** their behavior is unchanged. The new route is checked before the `/items/<id>` pattern, and a non-GET request to `/items/low-stock` still gets the usual `404`.\n- **Code changes:** I added a `parse_threshold` helper in `inventory/app.py` using only the standard library. In `tests/test_app.py`, the `call` helper gained an optional `query` argument and I added a `LowStockTests` class.\n- **Tests:** they cover the default and explicit thresholds, the strict cutoff, the sort order, the item fields, the bad inputs, and that `/items` and `/items/<id>` still work.\n\nI haven't committed anything.","ttft_ms":2620,"type":"result","duration_ms":28629,"uuid":"3c05b107-594b-4f10-8ee0-0f548790b78a","ttft_stream_ms":1912,"time_to_request_ms":47,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":14,"system_prompt":8,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":1,"input_attachments":6,"input_hooks":0,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":2,"engine_pickup":1,"autocompact":1,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":6,"message_normalization":1,"client_creation":2,"request_build":3},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":0,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":65,"time_to_request_major_faults":73,"first_content_frame_ms":1913,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
